    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An Ottoman province founded by the Barbarossa brothers, which became a largely self-governing corsair state ruled by elected deys.</li><li>Corsairing, captive ransoms and tribute from European states paid for a small Turkish military elite that ruled a mostly rural <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a>.</li><li>It defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> in 1541 but was crippled by bombardments in 1815–1816 and conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1830.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-de-cervantes">Miguel de Cervantes</a> spent five years as a captive in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> and tried to escape four times before Trinitarian friars ransomed him in 1580.</p></aside>
    </section>

