ror">Charles V</a>’s expedition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> is wrecked by a storm and repulsed</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1671</span><span class="rf-text">The corsair captains impose the first dey</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1708</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> takes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, losing it in 1732 and recovering it in 1792</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1816</span><span class="rf-text">An Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-pellew-1st-viscount-exmouth">Lord Exmouth</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombard">bombards</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1830</span><span class="rf-text">French troops land at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidi-fredj">Sidi Ferruch</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> capitulates on 5 July</span></li></ol>
